## What sess389 did

**Root fixed and verified — the publication-durability gate (0.19.40).** One measured chain on two nodes: a committed unlink conversion on a PR-held inode was *laundered* by xfsaild's P119 gate (marked clean, never written) → the release converter trusted `xfs_inode_clean` → the reload kept the newer in-core but *discharged the ledger* and stripped `LOCAL_UNLINK` → inactivation skipped the ifree → the AGI list named a LINKED dinode forever → `P88-PUBOB-UNREPAIRED`×60/node, 4 s deferral per AG release → aged-lap `dirent_durability` FAIL + the fossil `di_next_unlinked` family. GPT-ruled fix set F1–F4 landed (`xfs_inode.c` P55B PUBOB-at-PR flush, converter re-log repair + honest rc, `xfs_mxfs_dlm.c` no discharge on kept-ahead reloads, LOCAL_UNLINK cleared only on real adopt). Verified: 8+ aged 32-node laps all green (0.19.39 failed lap 3), fleet counters zero on every bad probe, **fault-injected launders 3/3 repaired**, P86 publish totals 245/245 joint, full board 27 PASS. **D-FOSSIL-NEXT-UNLINKED-IGET-LOGSAME-388 closed FIXED AND VERIFIED** (52 open).

**Geometry (0.20.0):** mkfs warns when `agcount < nodes` with the minimum device size; the kernel warns `P-AGCOUNT-COLLISION` at join (exactly slots 25–31 fired at 25 AGs); `mkfs_mxfs -d SIZE` + `MXFS_MKFS_OPTS` prep passthrough to reproduce geometries.

**The honest negative:** the 25-AG correctness retest **failed** — the two shared-AG slots wedged (`P-NOINO-RELFENCE-WEDGE`, #474 family: ILOCK held across the shared-AG CAW poll) and one split was published. `agcount < nodes` is not correctness-supported; PACE-388 and #474 stay open with the evidence (`tests/logs/ag25_incident_sess389.txt`).

**AGI chain-walk audit:** after quiescing all 32 nodes, `chk_mxfs -v` (now lists members) walked every chain clean; the 3 leftovers are cross-node open-unlink zombies awaiting their slot's remount — ledgered under the open-unlink entry.

